{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"0f58aa9dc98896471111b500a9722872d38728aaea8b27c826beceaf226b4365","digest":{"component_or_area":"close gate verifier and agent documentation","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:183","verify_completion","docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md","docs/llm-framework.md","CLAUDE.md","CLAUDE.local.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","transition … closed"],"problem_keywords":["close gate","verification","worktree","checkout","HEAD","working directory","agent guidance"],"propositions":["The close gate verifies the committed HEAD of the checkout from which the close command is invoked, not origin/main or the main checkout root, and this behavior is undocumented or misleading.","Agents create worktrees for edits but run close commands from the root checkout, causing the verifier to read the wrong (unchanged) tree.","Documentation must clearly state that close-gate verification reviews the committed HEAD of the invoking checkout/worktree and that agents must run close from the worktree containing the code to be verified.","Agent guidance (repo rules and skills) must instruct agents to cd into created worktrees and run all subsequent commands (edits, gates, rebar, close, git) from inside them.","The 'cwd/branch decoupling' statement in repo-snapshot-gates.md contradicts the ref=HEAD close path and must be reconciled so HEAD is resolved relative to the invoking checkout."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825163931386936,"uuid":"5cb599a8-4194-45f4-bed6-4b83dbc751c8"}